 "title": "Welcome to Ellsworth County, KS",
 "text": "Welcome to Ellsworth County, KS\nGO\nSearch\nHome\nGovernment\nCounty Attorney\nCounty Commissioners\nCounty Clerk\nDistrict Court\nCounty Register of Deeds\nSheriff's Office\nCo Treasurer - DMV & Property Tax\nDepartments\nAppraisers\nEconomic Development\nEmergency Management\nEMS\nMidway Extension District 15\nHealth Department\nRoad and Bridge\nResidents\nArchives\nCounty Information\nElections\nCounty Bulletin Board\nMajor Employers\nNoxious Weed & Landfill\nRecycling\nTownships\nNews & Job Openings\nProperty Taxes\nCo Treasurer - DMV & Property Tax\nSub Menu\nRelated\nPages\nTreasurer\nProperty Taxes\nDriver's License Contact Info\n50 State's Certificates\nCommonly Used Forms\nLevy Sheets\nQuarterly Reports\nHome › Government › Co Treasurer - DMV & Property Tax › Property Taxes\nReal Estate & Personal Property Taxes\nTax bills are mailed out in November of each year. The first half of taxes are due December 20th and\nthe second half is due May 10th the following year.\nClick for Public Property Tax Search\nFor Questions Regarding:\nReal Estate Value or the Neighborhood Revitalization Program,\ncontact Kimberly at 785-472-3165 or email khoyt@ellsworthcountyks.gov\nPersonal Property or oil & gas, contact Marie at 785-472-3165 or\nemail mranker@ellsworthcountyks.gov\nOnline Payment of Property Taxes\nTaxpayers can go to www.Kansas.gov/propertytax and select (Ellsworth County). Simply follow the instructions on\nthe screen. Two payment options, credit card or electronic check are available. This service allows for 24/7 secure\npayment access from any Internet connection. Payments cannot be made online if it is past the due date.\nInformation on Tax Lien Sale Overpayments\nEllsworth County held a tax lien sale in October of 2019. The starting bid for each property was one dollar. Two properties sold for amounts that would pay the taxes with an overage. The overage in the amount of $3,066.81 was awarded back to the property owner by court order. The overage of $466.48 was sent to the State of Kansas, Unclaimed Property Division February 12, 2020.\nEllsworth County held a tax lien sale November 9, 2023. The starting bid for each property was one dollar. One property sold for an amount that would pay the taxes with an overage. The overage in the amount of $309.42 was awarded back to the property owner by court order. The County Treasurer made due diligence trying to reach the property owner. The overage of $309.42 was sent to the State of Kansas, Unclaimed Property Division January of 2025.\n© 2017 Ellsworth County, KS\n210 N Kansas Ave Ellsworth KS 67439\nPowered By\nRevize\nLogin\n×\nShare this page\nCopy and past this code into your website.\n<a href=\"http://ellsworthcounty.org/government/treasurer/property_taxes.php\">Your Link Name</a>\nShare this page on your favorite Social network\nFacebook\nTwitter\nGoogle Plus\nReddit\nClose",
